From 52e50af61dfd37fdbf01736909febb0146ec8f03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Opus 5.5" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:47:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Build on FreeBSD (WSL guest): Hyper-V sockets, no Linux-only
 headers

- backend-rdp: create_vsock_fd() with AF_HYPERV on FreeBSD (Hyper-V sockets
  are what the WSL host connects to); gettid -> pthread_getthreadid_np(),
  fallocate -> posix_fallocate(); environ dump only on Linux (FreeBSD keeps
  environ in crt1.o, not visible to a -z defs shared object);
- launcher-direct and launcher-weston-launch only on Linux (linux/vt.h); the
  RDP backend uses no launcher;
- rdprail-shell: no mount namespaces on FreeBSD (setns/unshare skipped);
- portability: program_invocation_short_name -> getprogname(), ETIME,
  CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW, values.h, linux/limits.h, linux/ioctl.h and
  linux/types.h in the sync-file UAPI header, missing signal.h/float.h/libgen.h.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
